    4. For each hole-free object, generate a random 4-connected shape with NO interior hole.
       Can be small (1-2 px) or larger irregular shapes. Verify no hole via binary_fill_holes.
    5. Place all objects on the grid ensuring 4-connected separation (no two objects merge)
       and approximate bbox non-overlap. Fill remaining cells with bg.
    6. Output = copy input, recolor hole-containing objects to teal.
